  "priorExpiration": "2009-11-11",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 5011.04 Arrangement and Display. Containers of display fireworks shall be stored by being laid flat with top sides up. Corresponding sizes, grades, and brands shall be stored together within a magazine in such a manner that size, grade, and brand marks are easily visible upon inspection. Stocks of display fireworks shall be stored so as to be easily counted and checked.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at Chapter Heading for Saf-C 5000) #6055, eff 7-1-95; ss by #7481, eff 4-25-01, EXPIRED: 4-25-09\n\nNew. #9471, INTERIM, eff 5-15-09, EXPIRED: 11-11-09\n\nNew. #9765-A, eff 8-2-10; ss by #12738, eff 4-30-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c5000.html"
